**Usage:**

```tsx
// Basic — uses built-in fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary
  fallback={(error, reset) => (
    <div>
      <p>Oops: {error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
  onError={(error, info) => sentryClient.captureException(error, { extra: info })}
>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Key details:**
- `getDerivedStateFromError` — captures the error into state to trigger the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` — logs to console and calls the optional `onError` prop (hook for Sentry, Datadog, etc.)
- `reset` — clears error state, causing React to re-render children from scratch
- `fallback` prop — override the default UI entirely; receives `error` and `reset` for full control
- `role="alert"` — makes the fallback accessible to screen readers
